  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-25T23:44:52.097Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The SFX for the VR Camera controls have their volume handled by the World volume slider and it would make more sense for it to be controlled by the UI/Menu slider.\nExample scenario where this is bothersome: When trying to stream/record an event, it is useful to be able to mute UI/Menu sounds to prevent distracting viewers with seemingly random sounds (When using the stream camera). \nWith the Camera controls however, any time you want to change settings on it, your output media will contain the button sounds unless you also mute the World volume which is not always an option.\nSteps to reproduce: \n1. Mute UI/Menu audio\n2. Mess around with the VR Camera buttons\nExpected Result: VR Camera controls are muted.\nResult: You will still hear all the SFXs\nVRChat Version: 1191",
